Python + Redis.

Write a Python program to:
a.Connect to Redis running on localhost.
b.Store your name, age, and city using separate keys.
c.Retrieve and display the values.
d.Check whether the key name exists.
e.Delete the age key.

Step 1 — Install Redis Python library
!pip install redis

Step 2 — Connect to Redis
import redis
r = redis.Redis( host="localhost", port=6379, decode_responses=True
)
print("Connected to Redis")

Step 3 — Store name, age and city
r.set("name", "Vimlesh")
r.set("age", 24)
r.set("city", "Navi Mumbai") print("Data stored successfully")


Step 4 — Retrieve and display the values
print("Name:", r.get("name"))
print("Age:", r.get("age"))
print("City:", r.get("city"))

Step 5 — Check whether name exists
if r.exists("name"): 
print("Name key exists")
else:
print("Name key does not exist")

Step 6 — Delete the age key
r.delete("age")

print("Age key deleted")

Verify:
print("Age:", r.get("age"))
